    "q-164278": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164278",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $x$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{5} & =-1 \\\\ (x+4)^{2} & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the hyperboloid does not intersect the $x$-axis.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
