    "q-164272": {
      "dom_id": "step-q164272",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
