    "q-36475": {
      "dom_id": "step-q36475",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(z-3)^{2}}{9}=1$, find its $x$-intercepts.",
      "worked_solution": "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+2)^{2}}{4}-\\frac{(0-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-5)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x-5 & =\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =5\\pm 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $x=2$ and $8.$\n\nTherefore,the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(2,0,0)$ and $(8,0,0).$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
